2. what is LiveServer?
   Live Server is a VS Code extension that starts a local development server and automatically refreshes the browser when
   we save changes to our code.
3. What is the <script> element?
   The <script> element is used to include or execute JavaScript code in an HTML document.
   Ex:-
   <script>
     console.log('Hello World');
   </script>
   This executes the JavaScript and prints Hello World in the browser Console.
4. What is the purpose of the <script> element?
   The <script> element is used to embed JavaScript code in HTML or load an external JavaScript file.
   --How do you include an external JavaScript file?
     <script src="app.js"></script>
   The browser loads and executes the JavaScript file.

5. What is the difference between inline and external JavaScript?
   Inline JavaScript: Code is written directly inside the HTML <script> element.
   External JavaScript: Code is maintained in a separate .js file and loaded using the src attribute.

6. What is the difference between async and defer?
   <script src="app.js" defer></script>
   async: Downloads the script while HTML parsing continues and executes it as soon as it is ready.
   defer: Downloads the script while HTML parsing continues but executes it after HTML parsing finishes. Deferred scripts
   execute in document order.

7. Where should we place the <script> element?
   It can be placed in the <head> or <body>. Using defer in the <head> is a common approach for external scripts that
   need the HTML document to be parsed first.

